    'The International Space Station <select class="pte-select" data-answer="operates"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="operated">operated</option><option value="operating">operating</option><option value="operate">operate</option><option value="operates">operates</option></select> as a joint project among several countries\' space agencies. It orbits the Earth at an altitude of roughly four hundred <select class="pte-select" data-answer="kilometers"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="miles">miles</option><option value="kilometers">kilometers</option><option value="meters">meters</option><option value="centimeters">centimeters</option></select> above the surface. Astronauts aboard the station conduct experiments that would be <select class="pte-select" data-answer="impossible"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="impossible">impossible</option><option value="convenient">convenient</option><option value="simple">simple</option><option value="ordinary">ordinary</option></select> to perform on Earth. The station requires regular cargo missions to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="supply"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="supply">supply</option><option value="supplying">supplying</option><option value="supplies">supplies</option><option value="supplied">supplied</option></select> its crew with food, fuel, and equipment.',
    'Gravitational waves are ripples in spacetime that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="occur"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="occurring">occurring</option><option value="occurs">occurs</option><option value="occur">occur</option><option value="occurred">occurred</option></select> when massive objects accelerate. Albert Einstein <select class="pte-select" data-answer="predicted"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="predicting">predicting</option><option value="predicted">predicted</option><option value="predicts">predicts</option><option value="predict">predict</option></select> their existence a century before they were directly detected. In 2015, scientists finally <select class="pte-select" data-answer="detected"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="detecting">detecting</option><option value="detects">detects</option><option value="detected">detected</option><option value="detect">detect</option></select> gravitational waves produced by two colliding black holes. This discovery opened up an entirely new <select class="pte-select" data-answer="method"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="limitation">limitation</option><option value="restriction">restriction</option><option value="method">method</option><option value="obstacle">obstacle</option></select> of observing the universe beyond light-based astronomy.',
    'The discovery of antibiotics in the twentieth century <select class="pte-select" data-answer="represented"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="represent">represent</option><option value="representing">representing</option><option value="represents">represents</option><option value="represented">represented</option></select> one of the greatest advances in medical history. However, the overuse of these drugs has <select class="pte-select" data-answer="accelerated"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="accelerated">accelerated</option><option value="delayed">delayed</option><option value="prevented">prevented</option><option value="reversed">reversed</option></select> the emergence of resistant bacterial strains. Scientists now warn that some infections are becoming increasingly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="difficult"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="convenient">convenient</option><option value="difficult">difficult</option><option value="simple">simple</option><option value="affordable">affordable</option></select> to treat. Public health officials continue to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="advocate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="advocate">advocate</option><option value="advocated">advocated</option><option value="advocating">advocating</option><option value="advocates">advocates</option></select> the responsible use of antibiotics worldwide.',
