    'Insulin is a hormone that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="controls"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="controlled">controlled</option><option value="controls">controls</option><option value="control">control</option><option value="controlling">controlling</option></select> the body\'s regulation of blood glucose levels. In type 1 diabetes, the pancreas fails to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="produce"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="absorb">absorb</option><option value="store">store</option><option value="excrete">excrete</option><option value="produce">produce</option></select> sufficient insulin. Without proper management, chronically high blood sugar can cause <select class="pte-select" data-answer="severe"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="superficial">superficial</option><option value="temporary">temporary</option><option value="severe">severe</option><option value="minimal">minimal</option></select> damage to nerves and blood vessels. Many patients now use continuous glucose monitors to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="manage"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="manage">manage</option><option value="managed">managed</option><option value="manages">manages</option><option value="managing">managing</option></select> their condition more effectively.',
    'Vitamin D plays a <select class="pte-select" data-answer="vital"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="negligible">negligible</option><option value="trivial">trivial</option><option value="vital">vital</option><option value="minor">minor</option></select> role in maintaining strong bones and a healthy immune system. The human body <select class="pte-select" data-answer="synthesizes"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="synthesizes">synthesizes</option><option value="eliminates">eliminates</option><option value="stores">stores</option><option value="depletes">depletes</option></select> vitamin D naturally when skin is exposed to sunlight. A deficiency in this vitamin has been <select class="pte-select" data-answer="linked"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="links">links</option><option value="link">link</option><option value="linked">linked</option><option value="linking">linking</option></select> to conditions such as rickets and osteoporosis. Nutritionists therefore recommend that people <select class="pte-select" data-answer="obtain"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="obtained">obtained</option><option value="obtaining">obtaining</option><option value="obtains">obtains</option><option value="obtain">obtain</option></select> adequate sun exposure or dietary supplementation.',
    'Sleep is essential for the body to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="recover"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="recovers">recovers</option><option value="recover">recover</option><option value="recovered">recovered</option><option value="recovering">recovering</option></select> and repair itself. During deep sleep, the brain <select class="pte-select" data-answer="consolidates"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="distorts">distorts</option><option value="ignores">ignores</option><option value="erases">erases</option><option value="consolidates">consolidates</option></select> memories and clears metabolic waste products. Chronic sleep deprivation has been linked to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="impaired"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="stable">stable</option><option value="superior">superior</option><option value="impaired">impaired</option><option value="enhanced">enhanced</option></select> cognitive performance and weakened immunity. Experts therefore <select class="pte-select" data-answer="recommend"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="recommending">recommending</option><option value="recommends">recommends</option><option value="recommended">recommended</option><option value="recommend">recommend</option></select> that adults aim for seven to nine hours of sleep each night.',
    'Depression is a common mental health condition that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="affects"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="affect">affect</option><option value="affects">affects</option><option value="affected">affected</option><option value="affecting">affecting</option></select> millions of people worldwide. Unlike ordinary sadness, clinical depression tends to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="persist"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="fade">fade</option><option value="vanish">vanish</option><option value="subside">subside</option><option value="persist">persist</option></select> for weeks or months at a time. Effective treatments, including therapy and medication, can significantly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="alleviate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="alleviate">alleviate</option><option value="ignore">ignore</option><option value="provoke">provoke</option><option value="worsen">worsen</option></select> symptoms for most patients. Public awareness campaigns have <select class="pte-select" data-answer="helped"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="help">help</option><option value="helps">helps</option><option value="helping">helping</option><option value="helped">helped</option></select> reduce the stigma surrounding mental illness.',
    'Cancer occurs when abnormal cells <select class="pte-select" data-answer="divide"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="divide">divide</option><option value="divided">divided</option><option value="divides">divides</option><option value="dividing">dividing</option></select> uncontrollably and invade surrounding tissue. Early detection through screening can dramatically <select class="pte-select" data-answer="improve"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="limit">limit</option><option value="reduce">reduce</option><option value="improve">improve</option><option value="worsen">worsen</option></select> survival rates for many cancer types. Chemotherapy works by targeting cells that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="multiply"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="multiplying">multiplying</option><option value="multiplied">multiplied</option><option value="multiplies">multiplies</option><option value="multiply">multiply</option></select> rapidly, a hallmark of cancerous growth. Researchers remain <select class="pte-select" data-answer="optimistic"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="optimistic">optimistic</option><option value="pessimistic">pessimistic</option><option value="doubtful">doubtful</option><option value="indifferent">indifferent</option></select> that continued advances in immunotherapy will improve outcomes further.',
    'The kidneys <select class="pte-select" data-answer="filter"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="filtering">filtering</option><option value="filter">filter</option><option value="filtered">filtered</option><option value="filters">filters</option></select> waste products and excess fluid from the bloodstream. When kidney function declines severely, waste products can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="accumulate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="diminish">diminish</option><option value="dissipate">dissipate</option><option value="accumulate">accumulate</option><option value="evaporate">evaporate</option></select> dangerously in the blood. Dialysis is a medical procedure that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="performs"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="performing">performing</option><option value="perform">perform</option><option value="performed">performed</option><option value="performs">performs</option></select> the function of failing kidneys artificially. For many patients with end-stage renal disease, a kidney transplant offers a more permanent <select class="pte-select" data-answer="solution"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="solution">solution</option><option value="complication">complication</option><option value="obstacle">obstacle</option><option value="distraction">distraction</option></select> than long-term dialysis.',
    'Asthma is a chronic respiratory condition that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="causes"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="causes">causes</option><option value="causing">causing</option><option value="caused">caused</option><option value="cause">cause</option></select> the airways to narrow and become inflamed. Common triggers include allergens, cold air, and exercise, which can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="provoke"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="provoke">provoke</option><option value="cure">cure</option><option value="relieve">relieve</option><option value="prevent">prevent</option></select> sudden breathing difficulty. Inhaled corticosteroids help to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="reduce"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="reduces">reduces</option><option value="reducing">reducing</option><option value="reduced">reduced</option><option value="reduce">reduce</option></select> airway inflammation over the long term. With proper management, most people with asthma can lead <select class="pte-select" data-answer="healthy"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="healthy">healthy</option><option value="sedentary">sedentary</option><option value="restricted">restricted</option><option value="fragile">fragile</option></select> and active lives.',
    'At the height of summer the Arctic, tourist ships move gently around the coast. Even 10 years ago such sights would have been unthinkable, but today people are willing to pay large sums of money to see the last real wilderness in the world. In the Ice Caps, careless human exploitation <select class="pte-select" data-answer="has damaged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="have damaged">have damaged</option><option value="has damaged">has damaged</option><option value="damaging">damaging</option><option value="damage">damage</option></select> the fragile ecosystem. Today concerned governments are trying to find ways to develop the region <select class="pte-select" data-answer="in the future"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="in the future">in the future</option><option value="ever before">ever before</option><option value="in the past">in the past</option><option value="on one side">on one side</option></select> special natural environment. <select class="pte-select" data-answer="Although"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="Because">Because</option><option value="Since">Since</option><option value="Although">Although</option><option value="When">When</option></select> the Arctic is less accessible than the Ice Caps, it is still largely undamaged by humans.',
    'Myopia, or nearsightedness, occurs when the eye <select class="pte-select" data-answer="focuses"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="absorbs">absorbs</option><option value="focuses">focuses</option><option value="reflects">reflects</option><option value="blocks">blocks</option></select> light incorrectly onto a point in front of the retina. Prolonged near work, such as reading, has been <select class="pte-select" data-answer="associated"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="associated">associated</option><option value="associating">associating</option><option value="associates">associates</option><option value="associate">associate</option></select> with increased risk of myopia in children. Spending time outdoors appears to have a <select class="pte-select" data-answer="protective"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="protective">protective</option><option value="irritating">irritating</option><option value="negligible">negligible</option><option value="harmful">harmful</option></select> effect against the development of myopia. Corrective lenses or surgery can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="correct"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="correct">correct</option><option value="corrected">corrected</option><option value="correcting">correcting</option><option value="corrects">corrects</option></select> the refractive error and restore clear vision.',
    'Osteoporosis is a condition in which bones <select class="pte-select" data-answer="lose"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="losing">losing</option><option value="lose">lose</option><option value="loses">loses</option><option value="lost">lost</option></select> density and become fragile over time. The disease is particularly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="prevalent"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="temporary">temporary</option><option value="rare">rare</option><option value="prevalent">prevalent</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option></select> among postmenopausal women due to declining estrogen levels. Weight-bearing exercise has been shown to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="preserve"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="preserves">preserves</option><option value="preserve">preserve</option><option value="preserved">preserved</option><option value="preserving">preserving</option></select> bone strength and slow mineral loss. Adequate intake of calcium and vitamin D remains <select class="pte-select" data-answer="essential"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option><option value="harmful">harmful</option><option value="essential">essential</option><option value="optional">optional</option></select> for maintaining skeletal health throughout life.',
    'The human gut <select class="pte-select" data-answer="hosts"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="host">host</option><option value="hosted">hosted</option><option value="hosts">hosts</option><option value="hosting">hosting</option></select> trillions of bacteria that aid digestion and support immunity. A diverse microbiome has been <select class="pte-select" data-answer="linked"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="links">links</option><option value="link">link</option><option value="linking">linking</option><option value="linked">linked</option></select> to numerous benefits, including improved metabolic health. Diets high in processed foods can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="disrupt"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="strengthen">strengthen</option><option value="disrupt">disrupt</option><option value="restore">restore</option><option value="preserve">preserve</option></select> the balance of beneficial and harmful gut bacteria. Researchers increasingly view the microbiome as <select class="pte-select" data-answer="integral"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="integral">integral</option><option value="incidental">incidental</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option><option value="peripheral">peripheral</option></select> to overall human health rather than a passive bystander.',
    'At the height of summer the Patagonia, tourist ships move gently around the coast. Even 30 years ago such sights would have been unthinkable, but today people are willing to pay large sums of money to see the last real wilderness in the world. In the Northern Hemisphere, careless human exploitation <select class="pte-select" data-answer="has damaged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="have damaged">have damaged</option><option value="has damaged">has damaged</option><option value="damaging">damaging</option><option value="damage">damage</option></select> the fragile ecosystem. Today concerned governments are trying to find ways to develop the region <select class="pte-select" data-answer="in the future"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="in the future">in the future</option><option value="ever before">ever before</option><option value="in the past">in the past</option><option value="on one side">on one side</option></select> special natural environment. <select class="pte-select" data-answer="Although"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="Because">Because</option><option value="Since">Since</option><option value="Although">Although</option><option value="When">When</option></select> the Patagonia is less accessible than the Northern Hemisphere, it is still largely undamaged by humans.',
    'The discovery of blood types in the early twentieth century <select class="pte-select" data-answer="made"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="making">making</option><option value="made">made</option><option value="makes">makes</option><option value="make">make</option></select> transfusion medicine possible. Karl Landsteiner\'s identification of the ABO blood group system <select class="pte-select" data-answer="explained"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="explained">explained</option><option value="overlooked">overlooked</option><option value="questioned">questioned</option><option value="disputed">disputed</option></select> why earlier transfusions had often failed. Mismatched blood transfusions can trigger a <select class="pte-select" data-answer="severe"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="beneficial">beneficial</option><option value="negligible">negligible</option><option value="severe">severe</option><option value="mild">mild</option></select> immune reaction that damages red blood cells. Modern blood banks now carefully <select class="pte-select" data-answer="screen"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="screening">screening</option><option value="screen">screen</option><option value="screened">screened</option><option value="screens">screens</option></select> donated blood before it is used in transfusions.',
    'The evolution of cognitive psychology has fundamentally changed how we understand the human mind. Historically, researchers believed that consciousness <select class="pte-select" data-answer="played"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="plays">plays</option><option value="playing">playing</option><option value="played">played</option><option value="play">play</option></select> a minor role. However, recent studies have demonstrated that it is <select class="pte-select" data-answer="crucial"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="trivial">trivial</option><option value="crucial">crucial</option><option value="optional">optional</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option></select> to the overall system. As we continue to explore this fascinating field, it becomes <select class="pte-select" data-answer="evident"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="evident">evident</option><option value="obscure">obscure</option><option value="doubtful">doubtful</option><option value="hidden">hidden</option></select> that our previous models were incomplete. Future breakthroughs will likely <select class="pte-select" data-answer="rely"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="rely">rely</option><option value="relying">relying</option><option value="relied">relied</option><option value="relies">relies</option></select> heavily on interdisciplinary collaboration.',
    'At the height of summer the Antarctic, tourist ships move gently around the coast. Even 10 years ago such sights would have been unthinkable, but today people are willing to pay large sums of money to see the last real wilderness in the world. In the Tundra, careless human exploitation <select class="pte-select" data-answer="has damaged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="have damaged">have damaged</option><option value="has damaged">has damaged</option><option value="damaging">damaging</option><option value="damage">damage</option></select> the fragile ecosystem. Today concerned governments are trying to find ways to develop the region <select class="pte-select" data-answer="in the future"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="in the future">in the future</option><option value="ever before">ever before</option><option value="in the past">in the past</option><option value="on one side">on one side</option></select> special natural environment. <select class="pte-select" data-answer="Although"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="Because">Because</option><option value="Since">Since</option><option value="Although">Although</option><option value="When">When</option></select> the Antarctic is less accessible than the Tundra, it is still largely undamaged by humans.',
    'Before the introduction of anesthesia, surgical procedures <select class="pte-select" data-answer="caused"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="causing">causing</option><option value="causes">causes</option><option value="caused">caused</option><option value="cause">cause</option></select> excruciating pain for patients. The first public demonstration of ether anesthesia in 1846 <select class="pte-select" data-answer="marked"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="delayed">delayed</option><option value="marked">marked</option><option value="concealed">concealed</option><option value="avoided">avoided</option></select> a turning point in surgical history. Modern anesthesia allows surgeons to perform <select class="pte-select" data-answer="complex"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="superficial">superficial</option><option value="careless">careless</option><option value="complex">complex</option><option value="brief">brief</option></select> operations without causing the patient distress. Anesthesiologists continuously <select class="pte-select" data-answer="monitor"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="monitor">monitor</option><option value="monitored">monitored</option><option value="monitors">monitors</option><option value="monitoring">monitoring</option></select> a patient\'s vital signs throughout surgery to ensure safety.',
    'The inner ear contains tiny hair cells that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="convert"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="converting">converting</option><option value="converted">converted</option><option value="converts">converts</option><option value="convert">convert</option></select> sound vibrations into electrical signals. Prolonged exposure to loud noise can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="damage"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="damage">damage</option><option value="preserve">preserve</option><option value="strengthen">strengthen</option><option value="restore">restore</option></select> these delicate hair cells irreversibly. Once destroyed, human hair cells cannot <select class="pte-select" data-answer="regenerate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="regenerating">regenerating</option><option value="regenerates">regenerates</option><option value="regenerate">regenerate</option><option value="regenerated">regenerated</option></select> , unlike those of some animals. Hearing aids and cochlear implants can help <select class="pte-select" data-answer="mitigate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="mitigate">mitigate</option><option value="worsen">worsen</option><option value="ignore">ignore</option><option value="provoke">provoke</option></select> the effects of hearing loss for many patients.',
    'The skin acts as a protective barrier that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="shields"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="shields">shields</option><option value="shielded">shielded</option><option value="shield">shield</option><option value="shielding">shielding</option></select> the body from environmental damage. Excessive exposure to ultraviolet radiation can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="damage"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="repair">repair</option><option value="damage">damage</option><option value="stabilize">stabilize</option><option value="strengthen">strengthen</option></select> the DNA within skin cells. Over time, this damage may increase the <select class="pte-select" data-answer="risk"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="prevention">prevention</option><option value="cure">cure</option><option value="benefit">benefit</option><option value="risk">risk</option></select> of developing skin cancer. Dermatologists therefore <select class="pte-select" data-answer="recommend"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="recommended">recommended</option><option value="recommend">recommend</option><option value="recommending">recommending</option><option value="recommends">recommends</option></select> the daily use of broad-spectrum sunscreen to reduce UV exposure.',
    'Epidemiologists <select class="pte-select" data-answer="study"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="study">study</option><option value="studying">studying</option><option value="studied">studied</option><option value="studies">studies</option></select> patterns of disease spread to identify outbreaks early. During an outbreak, contact tracing helps to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="reveal"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="conceal">conceal</option><option value="complicate">complicate</option><option value="reveal">reveal</option><option value="distort">distort</option></select> how an infection moves through a population. Timely quarantine measures can significantly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="limit"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="limiting">limiting</option><option value="limited">limited</option><option value="limit">limit</option><option value="limits">limits</option></select> the transmission of contagious diseases. International cooperation remains <select class="pte-select" data-answer="crucial"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="optional">optional</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option><option value="unnecessary">unnecessary</option><option value="crucial">crucial</option></select> for detecting and responding to global health emergencies.',
    'The Human Genome Project <select class="pte-select" data-answer="completed"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="completed">completed</option><option value="completes">completes</option><option value="completing">completing</option><option value="complete">complete</option></select> the complete sequence of human DNA in 2003. This achievement has since <select class="pte-select" data-answer="allowed"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="discouraged">discouraged</option><option value="allowed">allowed</option><option value="restricted">restricted</option><option value="prevented">prevented</option></select> researchers to identify genes associated with specific diseases. Genetic testing can now reveal an individual\'s <select class="pte-select" data-answer="predisposition"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="predisposition">predisposition</option><option value="recovery">recovery</option><option value="resistance">resistance</option><option value="immunity">immunity</option></select> to certain hereditary conditions. Personalized medicine aims to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="tailor"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="tailors">tailors</option><option value="tailored">tailored</option><option value="tailor">tailor</option><option value="tailoring">tailoring</option></select> treatments based on a patient\'s unique genetic profile.',
    'During resistance training, muscle fibers <select class="pte-select" data-answer="sustain"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="eliminate">eliminate</option><option value="repair">repair</option><option value="sustain">sustain</option><option value="prevent">prevent</option></select> microscopic damage that triggers repair and growth. This repair process has been <select class="pte-select" data-answer="tied"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="tied">tied</option><option value="tying">tying</option><option value="ties">ties</option><option value="tie">tie</option></select> to increases in muscle strength and size over time. Adequate protein intake is <select class="pte-select" data-answer="essential"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="optional">optional</option><option value="essential">essential</option><option value="harmful">harmful</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option></select> for supporting muscle recovery after exercise. Regular strength training can also help to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="improve"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="improved">improved</option><option value="improving">improving</option><option value="improves">improves</option><option value="improve">improve</option></select> bone density and metabolic health.',
    'Cognitive psychologists have long studied how the mind temporarily holds and manipulates information needed for complex tasks such as reasoning and comprehension. Baddeley and Hitch <select class="pte-select" data-answer="proposed"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="propose">propose</option><option value="proposing">proposing</option><option value="proposed">proposed</option><option value="proposes">proposes</option></select> a multi-component model of working memory in 1974. In this model, the phonological loop <select class="pte-select" data-answer="retains"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="generates">generates</option><option value="retains">retains</option><option value="discards">discards</option><option value="calculates">calculates</option></select> verbal and acoustic information for brief periods. Meanwhile, the visuospatial sketchpad is <select class="pte-select" data-answer="responsible"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="hesitant">hesitant</option><option value="unlikely">unlikely</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option><option value="responsible">responsible</option></select> for processing visual and spatial data. Modern research continues to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="examine"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="examines">examines</option><option value="examine">examine</option><option value="examined">examined</option><option value="examining">examining</option></select> how these subsystems interact with the central executive.',
    'Ivan Pavlov\'s experiments with dogs revealed how neutral stimuli can come to elicit reflexive responses through repeated pairing. He noticed that dogs began to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="secrete"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="secrete">secrete</option><option value="secreting">secreting</option><option value="secreted">secreted</option><option value="secretes">secretes</option></select> saliva at the sound of a bell alone. This process, known as classical conditioning, <select class="pte-select" data-answer="pairs"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="isolates">isolates</option><option value="separates">separates</option><option value="contrasts">contrasts</option><option value="pairs">pairs</option></select> a previously neutral stimulus with an unconditioned one. Over time, the bell became a conditioned stimulus that was <select class="pte-select" data-answer="strongly"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="rarely">rarely</option><option value="faintly">faintly</option><option value="doubtfully">doubtfully</option><option value="strongly">strongly</option></select> associated with food. Later psychologists <select class="pte-select" data-answer="applied"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="applied">applied</option><option value="applies">applies</option><option value="applying">applying</option><option value="apply">apply</option></select> these principles to explain phobias and emotional responses in humans.',
    'Leon Festinger introduced the concept of cognitive dissonance to describe the discomfort that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="arises"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="arises">arises</option><option value="arising">arising</option><option value="arose">arose</option><option value="arise">arise</option></select> when a person holds two conflicting beliefs. Individuals experiencing this tension are often motivated to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="adjust"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="ignore">ignore</option><option value="preserve">preserve</option><option value="publicize">publicize</option><option value="adjust">adjust</option></select> their attitudes or behavior to restore consistency. In one classic study, participants who were paid less to lie about a boring task reported <select class="pte-select" data-answer="subsequently"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="unfortunately">unfortunately</option><option value="accidentally">accidentally</option><option value="rarely">rarely</option><option value="subsequently">subsequently</option></select> enjoying it more. This finding suggested that insufficient external justification <select class="pte-select" data-answer="encourages"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="encouraging">encouraging</option><option value="encouraged">encouraged</option><option value="encourages">encourages</option><option value="encourage">encourage</option></select> internal attitude change.',
    'Jean Piaget proposed that children progress through four distinct stages of cognitive development as they <select class="pte-select" data-answer="interpret"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="ignore">ignore</option><option value="distrust">distrust</option><option value="interpret">interpret</option><option value="memorize">memorize</option></select> the world around them. During the sensorimotor stage, infants <select class="pte-select" data-answer="develop"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="developing">developing</option><option value="develops">develops</option><option value="develop">develop</option><option value="developed">developed</option></select> object permanence, the understanding that objects continue to exist even when out of sight. In the concrete operational stage, children begin to think logically about <select class="pte-select" data-answer="concrete"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="mythical">mythical</option><option value="imaginary">imaginary</option><option value="concrete">concrete</option><option value="fictional">fictional</option></select> events rather than only abstract ones. Critics have since <select class="pte-select" data-answer="questioned"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="questioning">questioning</option><option value="questions">questions</option><option value="questioned">questioned</option><option value="question">question</option></select> whether these stages occur as rigidly as Piaget originally described.',
    'Confirmation bias refers to the tendency to seek out information that <select class="pte-select" data-answer="supports"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="supports">supports</option><option value="supporting">supporting</option><option value="support">support</option><option value="supported">supported</option></select> one\'s existing beliefs. People affected by this bias often <select class="pte-select" data-answer="dismiss"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="dismiss">dismiss</option><option value="publish">publish</option><option value="memorize">memorize</option><option value="celebrate">celebrate</option></select> evidence that contradicts their opinions. This tendency can be particularly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="harmful"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="trivial">trivial</option><option value="harmful">harmful</option><option value="negligible">negligible</option><option value="welcome">welcome</option></select> in political and scientific debates. Researchers have <select class="pte-select" data-answer="shown"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="shows">shows</option><option value="shown">shown</option><option value="showing">showing</option><option value="show">show</option></select> that actively seeking disconfirming evidence can reduce this bias.',
    'The evolution of genetics has fundamentally changed how we understand the oceanic ecosystem. Historically, researchers believed that bacteria <select class="pte-select" data-answer="played"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="plays">plays</option><option value="playing">playing</option><option value="played">played</option><option value="play">play</option></select> a minor role. However, recent studies have demonstrated that it is <select class="pte-select" data-answer="crucial"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="trivial">trivial</option><option value="crucial">crucial</option><option value="optional">optional</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option></select> to the overall system. As we continue to explore this fascinating field, it becomes <select class="pte-select" data-answer="evident"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="evident">evident</option><option value="obscure">obscure</option><option value="doubtful">doubtful</option><option value="hidden">hidden</option></select> that our previous models were incomplete. Future breakthroughs will likely <select class="pte-select" data-answer="rely"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="rely">rely</option><option value="relying">relying</option><option value="relied">relied</option><option value="relies">relies</option></select> heavily on interdisciplinary collaboration.',
    'Sleep plays a critical role in strengthening newly formed memories, a process known as consolidation. During deep sleep, the brain <select class="pte-select" data-answer="transfers"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="transfers">transfers</option><option value="transferred">transferred</option><option value="transferring">transferring</option><option value="transfer">transfer</option></select> information from short-term to long-term storage. Studies have shown that rapid eye movement, or REM, sleep is particularly <select class="pte-select" data-answer="important"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="optional">optional</option><option value="insignificant">insignificant</option><option value="important">important</option><option value="harmful">harmful</option></select> for consolidating procedural and emotional memories. Sleep deprivation, by contrast, can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="impair"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="impairs">impairs</option><option value="impairing">impairing</option><option value="impair">impair</option><option value="impaired">impaired</option></select> the ability to retain newly learned material. Consequently, researchers <select class="pte-select" data-answer="recommend"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="forbid">forbid</option><option value="dismiss">dismiss</option><option value="recommend">recommend</option><option value="question">question</option></select> adequate sleep as essential for students preparing for exams.',
    'John Bowlby\'s attachment theory suggests that infants <select class="pte-select" data-answer="form"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="forms">forms</option><option value="forming">forming</option><option value="formed">formed</option><option value="form">form</option></select> strong emotional bonds with primary caregivers for survival. Mary Ainsworth later <select class="pte-select" data-answer="developed"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="develops">develops</option><option value="developed">developed</option><option value="develop">develop</option><option value="developing">developing</option></select> the \'Strange Situation\' procedure to classify different attachment styles. Securely attached children typically show <select class="pte-select" data-answer="minimal"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="minimal">minimal</option><option value="prolonged">prolonged</option><option value="extreme">extreme</option><option value="aggressive">aggressive</option></select> distress when reunited with a caregiver after separation. In contrast, insecurely attached children may <select class="pte-select" data-answer="resist"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="resisted">resisted</option><option value="resists">resists</option><option value="resisting">resisting</option><option value="resist">resist</option></select> comfort or show ambivalence toward the caregiver.',
    'B.F. Skinner argued that behavior is shaped by its consequences rather than by internal mental states. In his experiments, rats <select class="pte-select" data-answer="pressed"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="presses">presses</option><option value="pressing">pressing</option><option value="press">press</option><option value="pressed">pressed</option></select> a lever to receive a food pellet. This reward <select class="pte-select" data-answer="increased"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="increased">increased</option><option value="increasing">increasing</option><option value="increase">increase</option><option value="increases">increases</option></select> the likelihood that the behavior would be repeated. Skinner distinguished this process, called reinforcement, from punishment, which is intended to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="decrease"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="publicize">publicize</option><option value="celebrate">celebrate</option><option value="decrease">decrease</option><option value="memorize">memorize</option></select> the frequency of a behavior. His work laid the foundation for behavior modification techniques still <select class="pte-select" data-answer="used"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="use">use</option><option value="used">used</option><option value="uses">uses</option><option value="using">using</option></select> in clinical and educational settings today.',
    'The Dunning-Kruger effect describes a cognitive bias in which people with limited ability in a domain <select class="pte-select" data-answer="overestimate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="overestimating">overestimating</option><option value="overestimated">overestimated</option><option value="overestimates">overestimates</option><option value="overestimate">overestimate</option></select> their own competence. Because they lack the skill to recognize their own errors, these individuals often feel unjustifiably <select class="pte-select" data-answer="confident"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="confident">confident</option><option value="anxious">anxious</option><option value="indifferent">indifferent</option><option value="humiliated">humiliated</option></select>. Ironically, highly skilled individuals sometimes <select class="pte-select" data-answer="underestimate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="underestimate">underestimate</option><option value="underestimating">underestimating</option><option value="underestimates">underestimates</option><option value="underestimated">underestimated</option></select> their own abilities, assuming tasks are equally easy for others. Awareness of this effect has <select class="pte-select" data-answer="encouraged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="discouraged">discouraged</option><option value="prevented">prevented</option><option value="forbidden">forbidden</option><option value="encouraged">encouraged</option></select> people to seek external feedback rather than relying solely on self-assessment.',
    'At the height of summer the Arctic, tourist ships move gently around the coast. Even 20 years ago such sights would have been unthinkable, but today people are willing to pay large sums of money to see the last real wilderness in the world. In the Northern Hemisphere, careless human exploitation <select class="pte-select" data-answer="has damaged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="have damaged">have damaged</option><option value="has damaged">has damaged</option><option value="damaging">damaging</option><option value="damage">damage</option></select> the fragile ecosystem. Today concerned governments are trying to find ways to develop the region <select class="pte-select" data-answer="in the future"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="in the future">in the future</option><option value="ever before">ever before</option><option value="in the past">in the past</option><option value="on one side">on one side</option></select> special natural environment. <select class="pte-select" data-answer="Although"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="Because">Because</option><option value="Since">Since</option><option value="Although">Although</option><option value="When">When</option></select> the Arctic is less accessible than the Northern Hemisphere, it is still largely undamaged by humans.',
    'The bystander effect describes the phenomenon whereby individuals are less likely to help a victim when other people are <select class="pte-select" data-answer="present"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="informed">informed</option><option value="absent">absent</option><option value="present">present</option><option value="distant">distant</option></select>. Researchers Bibb Latané and John Darley <select class="pte-select" data-answer="studied"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="studies">studies</option><option value="study">study</option><option value="studying">studying</option><option value="studied">studied</option></select> this effect after the widely publicized murder of Kitty Genovese. They found that responsibility for helping tends to be <select class="pte-select" data-answer="diffused"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="concentrated">concentrated</option><option value="publicized">publicized</option><option value="diffused">diffused</option><option value="ignored">ignored</option></select> among multiple bystanders, reducing individual accountability. As a result, a lone witness is often more likely to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="offer"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="offers">offers</option><option value="offering">offering</option><option value="offered">offered</option><option value="offer">offer</option></select> assistance than someone in a crowd.',
    'The Stroop effect demonstrates how automatic cognitive processes can <select class="pte-select" data-answer="interfere"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="interfered">interfered</option><option value="interfering">interfering</option><option value="interferes">interferes</option><option value="interfere">interfere</option></select> with a person\'s ability to complete a task. In the classic task, participants are asked to name the <select class="pte-select" data-answer="color"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="color">color</option><option value="length">length</option><option value="meaning">meaning</option><option value="spelling">spelling</option></select> of a word rather than read the word itself. When the word and ink color conflict, such as the word \'red\' printed in blue, response times <select class="pte-select" data-answer="increase"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="increased">increased</option><option value="increases">increases</option><option value="increasing">increasing</option><option value="increase">increase</option></select> noticeably. This delay <select class="pte-select" data-answer="suggests"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="forbids">forbids</option><option value="denies">denies</option><option value="suggests">suggests</option><option value="disputes">disputes</option></select> that reading is a highly automatic process that is difficult to suppress.',
    'Long-term potentiation, or LTP, is a process by which synaptic connections <select class="pte-select" data-answer="become"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="become">become</option><option value="becoming">becoming</option><option value="becomes">becomes</option><option value="became">became</option></select> stronger with repeated stimulation. This strengthening is widely considered a cellular mechanism <select class="pte-select" data-answer="underlying"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="underlying">underlying</option><option value="replacing">replacing</option><option value="opposing">opposing</option><option value="ignoring">ignoring</option></select> learning and memory formation. LTP was first <select class="pte-select" data-answer="discovered"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="discovering">discovering</option><option value="discovered">discovered</option><option value="discover">discover</option><option value="discovers">discovers</option></select> in the hippocampus, a brain region crucial for forming new memories. Since then, researchers have <select class="pte-select" data-answer="identified"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="identified">identified</option><option value="disputed">disputed</option><option value="forbidden">forbidden</option><option value="eliminated">eliminated</option></select> similar mechanisms in other regions of the brain.',
    'Daniel Kahneman and Amos Tversky developed prospect theory to explain how people <select class="pte-select" data-answer="make"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="making">making</option><option value="make">make</option><option value="made">made</option><option value="makes">makes</option></select> decisions under conditions of risk and uncertainty. Their research showed that people tend to feel losses more <select class="pte-select" data-answer="intensely"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="intensely">intensely</option><option value="rarely">rarely</option><option value="indifferently">indifferently</option><option value="mildly">mildly</option></select> than equivalent gains. This asymmetry, known as loss aversion, <select class="pte-select" data-answer="explains"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="explained">explained</option><option value="explaining">explaining</option><option value="explain">explain</option><option value="explains">explains</option></select> many seemingly irrational financial decisions. Prospect theory has since been <select class="pte-select" data-answer="applied"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="applies">applies</option><option value="applying">applying</option><option value="applied">applied</option><option value="apply">apply</option></select> to fields ranging from economics to public health policy.',
