    'In 1983, economist Muhammad Yunus founded the Grameen Bank to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="provide"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="provided">provided</option><option value="providing">providing</option><option value="provides">provides</option><option value="provide">provide</option></select> small loans to the rural poor in Bangladesh. Unlike traditional banks, Grameen Bank did not require <select class="pte-select" data-answer="collateral"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="subsidies">subsidies</option><option value="dividends">dividends</option><option value="royalties">royalties</option><option value="collateral">collateral</option></select> from borrowers who had no assets to pledge. The bank\'s microfinance model proved especially <select class="pte-select" data-answer="empowering"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="punitive">punitive</option><option value="restrictive">restrictive</option><option value="irrelevant">irrelevant</option><option value="empowering">empowering</option></select> for women seeking to start small businesses. For his pioneering work, Yunus <select class="pte-select" data-answer="received"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="received">received</option><option value="receiving">receiving</option><option value="receives">receives</option><option value="receive">receive</option></select> the Nobel Peace Prize in 2006.',
    'By the late 19th century, John D. Rockefeller\'s Standard Oil <select class="pte-select" data-answer="controlled"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="controlled">controlled</option><option value="controls">controls</option><option value="control">control</option><option value="controlling">controlling</option></select> nearly the entire American oil refining industry. Critics argued that the company\'s dominance left little room for <select class="pte-select" data-answer="competition"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="regulation">regulation</option><option value="transparency">transparency</option><option value="collaboration">collaboration</option><option value="competition">competition</option></select>. In 1911, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that Standard Oil must be broken into <select class="pte-select" data-answer="separate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="temporary">temporary</option><option value="subsidiary">subsidiary</option><option value="separate">separate</option><option value="identical">identical</option></select> companies. This landmark antitrust case continues to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="shape"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="shaping">shaping</option><option value="shaped">shaped</option><option value="shape">shape</option><option value="shapes">shapes</option></select> how regulators approach corporate monopolies today.',
    'Venture capital firms <select class="pte-select" data-answer="provide"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="providing">providing</option><option value="provide">provide</option><option value="provided">provided</option><option value="provides">provides</option></select> early funding to startups in exchange for equity ownership. In return, investors expect that a small number of successful companies will deliver enormous <select class="pte-select" data-answer="returns"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="expenses">expenses</option><option value="liabilities">liabilities</option><option value="deficits">deficits</option><option value="returns">returns</option></select>. Silicon Valley became the <select class="pte-select" data-answer="leading"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="obsolete">obsolete</option><option value="leading">leading</option><option value="marginal">marginal</option><option value="declining">declining</option></select> hub of the global venture capital industry starting in the late 20th century. However, most startups that receive venture funding ultimately <select class="pte-select" data-answer="fail"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="fail">fail</option><option value="failed">failed</option><option value="failing">failing</option><option value="fails">fails</option></select> to achieve profitability.',
