    'Since the 1980s, many manufacturers have chosen to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="relocate"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="relocates">relocates</option><option value="relocated">relocated</option><option value="relocating">relocating</option><option value="relocate">relocate</option></select> production to countries with lower labor costs. This practice, often called outsourcing, has made consumer goods considerably more <select class="pte-select" data-answer="affordable"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="hazardous">hazardous</option><option value="affordable">affordable</option><option value="exclusive">exclusive</option><option value="scarce">scarce</option></select> in wealthy nations. Critics argue that outsourcing has caused significant <select class="pte-select" data-answer="declines"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="booms">booms</option><option value="gains">gains</option><option value="declines">declines</option><option value="surges">surges</option></select> in manufacturing employment across developed economies. Supporters counter that globalization has also <select class="pte-select" data-answer="lifted"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="lifted">lifted</option><option value="lifts">lifts</option><option value="lifting">lifting</option><option value="lift">lift</option></select> millions out of poverty in developing countries.',
    'The Industrial Revolution transformed textile production by <select class="pte-select" data-answer="replacing"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="replace">replace</option><option value="replaced">replaced</option><option value="replacing">replacing</option><option value="replaces">replaces</option></select> hand spinning with mechanized power looms. Factories powered by steam engines proved far more <select class="pte-select" data-answer="productive"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="unreliable">unreliable</option><option value="wasteful">wasteful</option><option value="obsolete">obsolete</option><option value="productive">productive</option></select> than traditional home workshops at producing cloth. This shift drew large numbers of rural workers into rapidly growing, and often <select class="pte-select" data-answer="overcrowded"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="spacious">spacious</option><option value="overcrowded">overcrowded</option><option value="deserted">deserted</option><option value="pristine">pristine</option></select>, industrial cities. Despite harsh working conditions, industrialization ultimately <select class="pte-select" data-answer="raised"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="raising">raising</option><option value="raise">raise</option><option value="rise">rise</option><option value="raised">raised</option></select> living standards across much of Europe over the long run.',
    'Psychologists Daniel Kahneman and Amos Tversky <select class="pte-select" data-answer="shaped"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="shape">shape</option><option value="shaped">shaped</option><option value="shapes">shapes</option><option value="shaping">shaping</option></select> the field of behavioral economics through decades of research on decision-making. Their work revealed that people often rely on mental shortcuts, or heuristics, that can lead to <select class="pte-select" data-answer="irrational"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="flawless">flawless</option><option value="irrational">irrational</option><option value="unanimous">unanimous</option><option value="calculated">calculated</option></select> decisions. One famous concept, loss aversion, shows that people feel losses more <select class="pte-select" data-answer="intensely"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="mildly">mildly</option><option value="rarely">rarely</option><option value="evenly">evenly</option><option value="intensely">intensely</option></select> than equivalent gains. These insights have <select class="pte-select" data-answer="challenged"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="challenge">challenge</option><option value="challenging">challenging</option><option value="challenged">challenged</option><option value="challenges">challenges</option></select> traditional economic models that assume humans always act rationally.',
    'The euro was <select class="pte-select" data-answer="introduced"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="introduced">introduced</option><option value="introduce">introduce</option><option value="introducing">introducing</option><option value="introduces">introduces</option></select> as the common currency of the European Union in 1999, initially for electronic transactions only. Physical euro coins and banknotes were not put into <select class="pte-select" data-answer="circulation"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="storage">storage</option><option value="production">production</option><option value="circulation">circulation</option><option value="reserve">reserve</option></select> until January 2002. Adopting a shared currency eliminated exchange-rate risk but also left member states with <select class="pte-select" data-answer="limited"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="expanded">expanded</option><option value="limited">limited</option><option value="flexible">flexible</option><option value="unanimous">unanimous</option></select> control over their own monetary policy. During the 2010 sovereign debt crisis, several eurozone countries <select class="pte-select" data-answer="faced"><option value="" disabled selected>Select Answer</option><option value="faces">faces</option><option value="facing">facing</option><option value="face">face</option><option value="faced">faced</option></select> severe financial difficulties.',
